80-building-a-legend?p=1097343#post1097343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this book is only available to supporters who pledged for a physical copy of Beast; Is there any way to get on that list retroactively?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Sorry.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, once errata is collected and it's prepared for print, it becomes available for everyone. So it's not completely out of your hands, it's just more time till it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T16:25:36-07:00","id":1097348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1097333#post1097333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. And Gotham, Gravity Falls, Lovecraft County, Genosha, and Stephen King's Maine all get called out in a sidebar of fictional settings to draw upon. That alone makes this one of my favourite short RPG books!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Gravity Falls reference made me so happy. Definitely a good sign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T01:59:13-07:00","id":1097461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1097333#post1097333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. And Gotham, Gravity Falls, Lovecraft County, Genosha, and Stephen King's Maine all get called out in a sidebar of fictional settings to draw upon. That alone makes this one of my favourite short RPG books!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey, don't forget about Night Vale. Everyone's favorite friendly desert community where the sun is hot, the moon is beautiful, and mysterious lights pass overhead while we all pretend to sleep. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T08:10:12-07:00","id":1097523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1097333#post1097333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. And Gotham, Gravity Falls, Lovecraft County, Genosha, and <b>Stephen King's Maine</b> all get called out in a sidebar of fictional settings to draw upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am laughing so hard right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T08:05:27-07:00","id":1097779,"title":"","content":"One thing I really like about this is the additional clarification on how the Primordial Dream works and why the advent of modern communications have made it such a mess to navigate. The core book talks about it, but Building a Legend really helps me understand how the Primordial Dream is supposed to correspond to local threats, only now we're adding fears from all over the world and inventing them whole cloth, which makes it nearly impossible to sift out true warnings from false. Great, we've given the whole world anxiety and when the alarm bells never cease you just learn to tune them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T17:17:32-07:00","id":1098290,"title":"","content":"The suspense is killing me! Can anyone out there give a rundown on the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T17:22:58-07:00","id":1098291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1098290#post1098290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The suspense is killing me! Can anyone out there give a rundown on the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its very solid. Haven't read all of it, but this is an extremely crossover-friendly book. I would recommend it for any gameline. You can easily build a Dark Era or signature location based on what's here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T07:20:54-07:00","id":1098757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1097523#post1097523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am laughing so hard right now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why? How come? Por que?<br /> <br /> (Forum software requires at least 10 characters.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T12:33:16-07:00","id":1098843,"title":"","content":"Reading it and finding it rather interesting so far! <br /> <br /> But I'm wondering if this might be a mistake? Page 35, under Invading Heroes and Horrors says... &quot;Many Heroes have ways of entering a Beast\u2019s Lair \u2014 and not just the Lair of the Beast that made them what they are.&quot; <br /> <br /> I thought Beast moved away from Beasts causing Heroes to be? Did I misunderstand something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:16:50-07:00","id":1098859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1098843#post1098843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading it and finding it rather interesting so far!<br /> <br /> But I'm wondering if this might be a mistake? Page 35, under Invading Heroes and Horrors says... &quot;Many Heroes have ways of entering a Beast\u2019s Lair \u2014 and not just the Lair of the Beast that made them what they are.&quot;<br /> <br /> I thought Beast moved away from Beasts causing Heroes to be? Did I misunderstand something?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, you're right. I suspect that's just bad phrasing, but do me a favor and put it in the errata thread and I'll fix it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:24:34-07:00","id":1098864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1098859#post1098859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, you're right. I suspect that's just bad phrasing, but do me a favor and put it in the errata thread and I'll fix it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And done. Glad to assist with that. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T14:08:19-07:00","id":1098889,"title":"","content":"Man... I really like the description of Chambers a lot more in Building a Legend. But I'm having a lot of trouble meshing what BaL talks about and the actual rules in the game. <br /> <br /> For example, there is a lot of talk about how wild Chambers are great resources that Beasts will fight over and contest each other in order to procure. It gives a great sense of conflict between Beasts, emphasizes territorial behavior which I like and I like the idea of Beasts wanting to hoard Chambers....<br /> <br /> But I don't really see how they can do that. Beasts are restricted in how many Chambers they can have by their Lair Trait and Lair 1-5 only afford 3/3/4/4/5. That's... Not a lot of room for options there... And it doesn't seem in character for Beasts to just fight over a Chamber, make it part of their Lair, only to just collapse that Chamber to make room for the new shiny Chamber in the area, yeah? It doesn't to me... <br /> <br /> Chambers are supposed to be very personal and reflect the growth of your Horror's Legend, I thought. So... <br /> <br /> Considering your first Chamber is always your Heart... And you start with a second Chamber... New characters are only going to have room for one more Chamber for awhile and that seems to encourage a young Beast to be picky, not trying to gobble up what territory they can... <br /> <br /> So... I'm kinda confused on the matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T07:36:00-07:00","id":1099146,"title":"","content":"You can start with just the Heart for 2XP. I always do that with my characters because it's fun and also comes with a handy first Aspiration: find a new Chamber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T08:30:18-07:00","id":1099162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1098889#post1098889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man... I really like the description of Chambers a lot more in Building a Legend. But I'm having a lot of trouble meshing what BaL talks about and the actual rules in the game.<br /> <br /> For example, there is a lot of talk about how wild Chambers are great resources that Beasts will fight over and contest each other in order to procure. It gives a great sense of conflict between Beasts, emphasizes territorial behavior which I like and I like the idea of Beasts wanting to hoard Chambers....<br /> <br /> But I don't really see how they can do that. Beasts are restricted in how many Chambers they can have by their Lair Trait and Lair 1-5 only afford 3/3/4/4/5. That's... Not a lot of room for options there... And it doesn't seem in character for Beasts to just fight over a Chamber, make it part of their Lair, only to just collapse that Chamber to make room for the new shiny Chamber in the area, yeah? It doesn't to me...<br /> <br /> Chambers are supposed to be very personal and reflect the growth of your Horror's Legend, I thought. So...<br /> <br /> Considering your first Chamber is always your Heart... And you start with a second Chamber... New characters are only going to have room for one more Chamber for awhile and that seems to encourage a young Beast to be picky, not trying to gobble up what territory they can...<br /> <br /> So... I'm kinda confused on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I suppose you can also collapse Chambers for protection when one's location has been compromised, or Heroes can collapse your Chambers on purpose.<br /> <br /> And there's whatever Insatiables can do too. So maybe the fight for Chambers as a resource is tougher in areas of heavy conflict?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T08:02:22-07:00","id":1099824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1098757#post1098757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why? How come? Por que?<br /> <br /> (Forum software requires at least 10 characters.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It just amuses me that Stephen King has set so many stories in Maine that it's become such a widespread meme. If you're from Quebec, Maine is just where you go on summer vacation if you can't go to Florida; my grandparents go there about every year. The dissonance between &quot;an okay-ish vacation spot that lets you tell people you went on vacation in the States without having to spend that much money&quot; and, say, <i>It</i>, is <i>just</i> jarring enough to be absurd to me. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T14:20:04-07:00","id":1100583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1098889#post1098889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man... I really like the description of Chambers a lot more in Building a Legend. But I'm having a lot of trouble meshing what BaL talks about and the actual rules in the game.<br /> <br /> For example, there is a lot of talk about how wild Chambers are great resources that Beasts will fight over and contest each other in order to procure. It gives a great sense of conflict between Beasts, emphasizes territorial behavior which I like and I like the idea of Beasts wanting to hoard Chambers....<br /> <br /> But I don't really see how they can do that. Beasts are restricted in how many Chambers they can have by their Lair Trait and Lair 1-5 only afford 3/3/4/4/5. That's... Not a lot of room for options there... And it doesn't seem in character for Beasts to just fight over a Chamber, make it part of their Lair, only to just collapse that Chamber to make room for the new shiny Chamber in the area, yeah? It doesn't to me...<br /> <br /> Chambers are supposed to be very personal and reflect the growth of your Horror's Legend, I thought. So...<br /> <br /> Considering your first Chamber is always your Heart... And you start with a second Chamber... New characters are only going to have room for one more Chamber for awhile and that seems to encourage a young Beast to be picky, not trying to gobble up what territory they can...<br /> <br /> So... I'm kinda confused on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea was to just provide differing options on how a Beast could acquire a Chamber. That finding a wild Chamber is one way to do so, and fighting another Beast to get also adds a story hook in addition to the new Chamber. <br /> <br /> Since even when a Beast's Lair trait gets increased and their Max amount of Chambers gets increased, they don't gain a new Chamber automatically. So this is one way of getting a new Chamber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T00:15:56-07:00","id":1100735,"title":"","content":"Did not read <b>Building the Legend</b> - but cannot Beast just fall it's previous Chamber, to make place for new Chamber won in fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T06:58:47-07:00","id":1100812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1100735#post1100735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did not read <b>Building the Legend</b> - but cannot Beast just fall it's previous Chamber, to make place for new Chamber won in fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Beast can collapse one of their own chambers, but the book presents it as a thing you do to protect yourself. Keep in mind, the Chambers of your Lair are pretty much your home and are meant to be representative of what you hunt and stalk in. <br /> <br /> It seems counterproductive to collapse a Chamber for no real reason. <br /> <br /> What are the reasons to willingly give up a Chamber?<br /> <br /> Legitimate question, that, to anyone interested in engaging with it. From what I understand, the only mechanical benefit a Chamber provides is the environmental Tilt it has. But that doesn't mean there aren't non-mechanical reasons to prefer one Chamber over another, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T14:06:24-07:00","id":1100955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1100812#post1100812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legitimate question, that, to anyone interested in engaging with it. From what I understand, the only mechanical benefit a Chamber provides is the environmental Tilt it has. But that doesn't mean there aren't non-mechanical reasons to prefer one Chamber over another, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only other major mechanical benefit is the bonus Satiety that comes from when you Feed in your Lair...and that's about it. <br /> <br /> Although collapsing a Chamber willingly while in the middle of combat, is a powerful move, since it either kills anyone still inside it or ejects them out through the nearest, open Primordial Pathway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T14:53:15-07:00","id":1100971,"title":"","content":"Opening Primordial Pathways is much easier to or from a place that is similar to a Chamber and even easier in the actual location a Chamber was formed as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T21:08:55-07:00","id":1101855,"title":"","content":"How well does this book work with making a city/setting without player involvement and without a group of PC's in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T23:25:46-07:00","id":1101870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1101855#post1101855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How well does this book work with making a city/setting without player involvement and without a group of PC's in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm...may I first ask why do you not want to factor in a group of PCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T23:37:15-07:00","id":1101873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1101870#post1101870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhm...may I first ask why do you not want to factor in a group of PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>My players trend to not make characters until after the setting had been made. <br /> <br /> Also, it means we can play after character creation rather than &quot;okay now that we've done character creation give me three weeks to make the setting&quot;, because I can make the setting and think up plot hooks before the game starts.<br /> <br /> Also it means that I can use the setting for future games better because it doesn't revolve around a specific group of characters who might die two sessions in...<br /> <br /> Also, I sort of enjoy making settings in the periods where my players are too busy to play, so on those situations the setting was never going to have PCs in it in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T10:46:36-07:00","id":1102036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1101873#post1101873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My players trend to not make characters until after the setting had been made.<br /> <br /> Also, it means we can play after character creation rather than &quot;okay now that we've done character creation give me three weeks to make the setting&quot;, because I can make the setting and think up plot hooks before the game starts.<br /> <br /> Also it means that I can use the setting for future games better because it doesn't revolve around a specific group of characters who might die two sessions in...<br /> <br /> Also, I sort of enjoy making settings in the periods where my players are too busy to play, so on those situations the setting was never going to have PCs in it in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok then. Uhm... <br /> <br /> -If you're reasonably confident and knowledgeable on what kind of game your players want, then yeah, you should be ok. Stuff like the Region building and creating the local Primordial Dream you should be fine with on your own. <br /> <br /> -Creating NPCs is obviously going to be different if you aren't building any that represent specific Social Merits for any of the PCs. Although BaL does offer the suggestion of just having a list of a bunch of NPCs, and only defining the bare minimum of stuff for them (personality traits, physical appearances, general overview of what Skills they're good at and what they're not-so-good at). And either just picking out an appropriate NPC when your PC calls upon one of their Social Merits, or asking your players to look over your NPC list to see what looks appropriate for them. <br /> <br /> -Since this is Beast, a good amount of text is devoted to crossovers with the other splats. But if you know fairly well which splats you want to bring in and which ones don't, as well as what your players feel about them without having any discussion, you should be ok. Or ignore the other splats completely if you're so inclined. <br /> <br /> Overall...yeah, a single ST should have no problem just making everything on their own. It'll require a lot more work, obviously, but it's doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T14:00:55-07:00","id":1102101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1098889#post1098889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man... I really like the description of Chambers a lot more in Building a Legend. But I'm having a lot of trouble meshing what BaL talks about and the actual rules in the game.<br /> <br /> For example, there is a lot of talk about how wild Chambers are great resources that Beasts will fight over and contest each other in order to procure. It gives a great sense of conflict between Beasts, emphasizes territorial behavior which I like and I like the idea of Beasts wanting to hoard Chambers....<br /> <br /> But I don't really see how they can do that. Beasts are restricted in how many Chambers they can have by their Lair Trait and Lair 1-5 only afford 3/3/4/4/5. That's... Not a lot of room for options there... And it doesn't seem in character for Beasts to just fight over a Chamber, make it part of their Lair, only to just collapse that Chamber to make room for the new shiny Chamber in the area, yeah? It doesn't to me...<br /> <br /> Chambers are supposed to be very personal and reflect the growth of your Horror's Legend, I thought. So...<br /> <br /> Considering your first Chamber is always your Heart... And you start with a second Chamber... New characters are only going to have room for one more Chamber for awhile and that seems to encourage a young Beast to be picky, not trying to gobble up what territory they can...<br /> <br /> So... I'm kinda confused on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but if you have a brood, it's 3 per member. So for your average brood of 5, there's a maximum of 15 chambers in the shared lair, of which 10 will be filled by your first chamber and your hearth. At Lair 3, you have 20 chambers max. That's actually a lot, I think. <br /> <br /> On a side note, any idea when BaL will be published for us non backers buyers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T04:22:31-07:00","id":1102230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1101873#post1101873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My players trend to not make characters until after the setting had been made.<br /> <br /> Also, it means we can play after character creation rather than &quot;okay now that we've done character creation give me three weeks to make the setting&quot;, because I can make the setting and think up plot hooks before the game starts.<br /> <br /> Also it means that I can use the setting for future games better because it doesn't revolve around a specific group of characters who might die two sessions in...<br /> <br /> Also, I sort of enjoy making settings in the periods where my players are too busy to play, so on those situations the setting was never going to have PCs in it in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think there's any particular reason you couldn't build a setting first and then fold the characters into it (or not). The thrust of the book is building a setting with the players, but I don't think it would break if you tried to do something else with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T04:54:57-07:00","id":1102235,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers tasti and Matt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T08:04:04-07:00","id":1102811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1097779#post1097779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I really like about this is the additional clarification on how the Primordial Dream works and why the advent of modern communications have made it such a mess to navigate. The core book talks about it, but Building a Legend really helps me understand how the Primordial Dream is supposed to correspond to local threats, only now we're adding fears from all over the world and inventing them whole cloth, which makes it nearly impossible to sift out true warnings from false. Great, we've given the whole world anxiety and when the alarm bells never cease you just learn to tune them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This much alone is enough to make me regret not backing for a physical copy to get a sooner look.<br /> <br /> Is there more information on Primordial Pathways in the book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T08:40:08-07:00","id":1102824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1096480-building-a-legend?p=1102811#post1102811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This much alone is enough to make me regret not backing for a physical copy to get a sooner look.<br /> <br /> Is there more information on Primordial Pathways in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not specifically on Primordial Pathways that I can discern. There's a good bit of discussion on Chambers, though, which is particularly related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}